    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gordĭānus</span></b> , i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman proper name;</i> in partic., the name of three Roman
			emperors, Capitol. Gord.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gordĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the emperor Gordian</i>, <i>Gordian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">LEGIO,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 53, 10</span></i>
			; Inscr. Don. cl. 3, <i>no.</i> 48.</div>
